is invented.\n\n**Landed on `main` outside the worker lifecycle**, via merge `13cac4e` of `aa2b263`:\n- `bf38be4`: durable materialization procedure plus the fail-closed read-back gate `tools/live/project_materialization.py`.\n- `62b85e0`: worker prompts name SWF-19 merge landing and forbid pull requests; Director comments are no longer reported as `INVALID_RESULT_COMMENT`.\n- `aa2b263`: repairs for an independent Codex review that returned REPAIR_REQUIRED (marker-attempt classification, board completeness).\n\n**Independent evaluation against this Issue's acceptance criteria**, re-run at `674b78d`:\n\n| Item | Status |\n|---|---|\n| Director comments misrouted as worker-result errors | **Satisfied** (`authority.mjs` `attemptsResultSignal`, dispatcher tests) |\n| AC4: PY-01–PY-10 compatibility and status vocabulary | **Satisfied** (`node scripts/check.mjs all` exit 0; dispatcher 155/155; materialization 12/12) |\n| Release-admission reader uses a stale shared checkout | **Not met.** The reader is `~/.local/share/alienintent-bootstrap/release_admission.py`, outside the repository. It still reads assessments from the working tree, not `origin/main`, and recognises only `PY-NN` and `WO-NNNNNN` records. Other BIUs fall back to the native-comment envelope. |\n| AC1: new BIU visible and tracked without a manual workaround | **Unproven.** No new BIU has been admitted without the fallback. |\n| AC2: command path reads the current durable source | **Partial.** The comment half is met; the durable-source half is not (see above). |\n| AC3: focused proof on a disposable fixture | **Partial.** Read-back only: #83 verifies (exit 0) and #85 fails closed (exit 1). |\n\n**Review custody:** `aa2b263` was merged 44 s after it was committed, with no independent re-review after REPAIR_REQUIRED. No ACCEPT record exists.\n\n**Also observed:** the GitHub Project add-path fault recorded on 2026-09-23 persists. #86 was created today, received an item ID, and is absent from the Project collection (count still 75). The read-back gate failed closed as designed.\n\n**Remaining work:**\n- The release-admission reader must read from `origin/main`, accept non-`WO` BIU records, and be brought under version control with tests. That is a code change, to be routed through the factory once it is in the repository.\n- A disposable-BIU admit proof.\n- An independent ACCEPT of the landed repair.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlienLogicLab/alienintent/issues/comments/5806704082/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"sanookdu","id":272393288,"node_id":"U_kgDOEDxkSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272393288?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanookdu","html_url":"https://github.com/sanookdu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanookdu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanookdu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanookdu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanookdu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanookdu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanookdu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanookdu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanookdu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanookdu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":31731947573,"node_id":"REFE_lADOUbjKuc8AAAABSviOd88AAAAHY18YNQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlienLogicLab/alienintent/issues/events/31731947573","actor":{"login":"sanookdu","id":272393288,"node_id":"U_kgDOEDxkSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272393288?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/u